From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Theo Paris <theo@theoparis.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 20:21:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] kernel: fix OSS/upstream-clang kernel bring-up

Fixes needed to build and boot a standalone kernel with upstream clang
and without Apple-silicon platform-expert support:

  * kalloc.h gains portable fallbacks for Apple Clang's
    __builtin_xnu_type_{summary,signature,types_compatible}.
  * vm_user.c supplies the plain-named MIG forwarding wrappers on all
    architectures and vm_map.defs skips the unimplemented routines.
  * memdev/mockfs carry a 64-bit memdev base.
  * bsd_init skips IOSecureBSDRoot on a ramdisk root, and
    pthread_functions is writable after machine_lockdown().
  * arm64 debug-trace gates and sleep asserts are relaxed for boards
    with no Apple platform expert.
